      "id": 1,
      "text": "Palmerton was named after New Jersey Zinc's president, Stephen S. Palmer, who resisted having the town bear his name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmerton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During the 19th century, Palmerton hosted an Underground Railroad station, offering a hidden refuge for escaping slaves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmerton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The New Jersey Zinc Company founded in 1897 built a smelting plant in Palmerton, turning the borough into a zinc mining hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmerton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Eastern European immigrants from Hungary, Poland, Russia, and Ukraine settled in Palmerton in the late 1800s, shaping its cultural fabric.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/1976437/palmerton-pennsylvania-charming-borough-eastern-european-heritage-river-rapids/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Palmerton Community Band, founded in 1911, still performs summer concerts in the borough park bandshell, keeping a century‑old tradition alive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palmerton%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Palmerton Area Heritage Center, run by the Historical Society, showcases exhibits that chronicle the town’s mining and immigrant history.",
